 },
 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:08:51.733869Z",
 "text": "Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* (RTA), rent increases in an ordinary private residential tenancy are governed by Part VII. \n\nSection 114(1) of the RTA provides that a landlord may increase the rent charged for a rental unit in accordance with Part VII. The specific statutory requirements of Part VII are:\n* **Notice:** At least 90 days' written notice in the approved Landlord and Tenant Board form (Section 116(1)).\n* **Frequency:** No more than once in any 12-month period (Section 119(1)).\n* **Amount:** Capped at the annual rent increase guideline unless an above-guideline increase is authorized (Section 120(1)).\n\nBecause the clause strictly restates and complies with these statutory requirements without contracting out of or violating the Act, it is valid and enforceable.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 114",
 "finish_reason": "STOP",
